# ==============================================================================
# 🔤 LINE ENDING NORMALISATION
# ==============================================================================
# This project is *nix-first: it runs under WSL, inside Docker, on a GCP VM and
# in the Ubuntu CI. All text is therefore stored AND checked out as LF, even on
# Windows.
#
# Why this file is essential:
# core.autocrlf is a GLOBAL machine setting (hence invisible in the repository).
# A Windows machine with autocrlf=true checks the working tree out as CRLF and
# normalises silently on read: git there reports "clean" while the files
# actually contain CR. Seen from WSL, the same tree appears entirely modified.
# The result: a single commit from WSL rewrites the whole repository.
# A .gitattributes rule is versioned, so it is identical everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Scripts and makefiles: LF IS MANDATORY. A CR breaks the shebang
# (`/bin/bash^M: bad interpreter`), fails heredocs, and contaminates variables
# (a value read from .env ends up suffixed with a \r).
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.bash      text eol=lf
Makefile    text eol=lf
*.mk        text eol=lf

# ==============================================================================
# 🖼️ BINARY FILES — no conversion, no textual diff
# ==============================================================================
*.pkl       binary
*.pickle    binary
*.joblib    binary
*.h5        binary
*.hdf5      binary
*.npz       binary
*.npy       binary
*.parquet   binary
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
*.ttf       binary
